Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||10-16-2000||12:46 PM||||Ok i have a 87 duke with 224,000 km on it and the motor feels like it is moving when i give it or release the gas or release it suddenly without releasing the clutch.  I had the dog bone replaced 6 months ago and all other motor mounts done a month later.  I feels loose and i brought it by the shop and another and they said it feels like they are tight<P>any help or suggestions would be great<BR>thanks <BR>kinboyatuwo||||reg||9
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||10-16-2000||01:27 PM||||I'm not sure, but didn't the pre '88s use some sort of rubber cradle mounts? mine's an '88 so I never really paid attention, but I thought I heard something about that. it could explain a bit. you could check for sure by having a friend sit in side, put it in drive and kreep the gas up while holding the break, if you're out back w/ the deck lid open, you would be able to visibly see it move and you may be able to see exactly where the flexing is at.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||10-16-2000||02:39 PM||||Since you said clutch I assume that it's a stick,if so just put it in gear on some level ground(brake and engine off) and rock the car back and forth and see if the engine moves. ||||reg||1
